  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p>
<i>Abramus abfens audiit, ilicet</i><br/>
<i>Vernas trecentos, bisque nouem simul</i><br/>
<i>Collegit, armis muniit, &amp; feros</i><br/>
<i>Sequutus hostes fortiter iruit,</i><br/>
<i>Et terga dantes funditus obruit.</i><br/>
<i>Potens supremi præsidio Patris.</i>
    </p>
    <p>
<i>Dehinc dura rupit vincula, &amp; aneas</i><br/>
<i>Vinctis catenas, &amp; decimis prius</i><br/>
<i>Summo solutis Pontifici sua</i><br/>
<i>Turba miselle restituit bona,</i><br/>
<i>Prædasque raptas. Sic rediit domum</i><br/>
<i>Victor decorus, totaque totius</i><br/>
<i>Orbis tremendo reddidit arbitro.</i>
    </p>
    <p>
<i>Quum tot niteret plena bonis domus,</i><br/>
<i>Gemmis &amp; auro, nec pareret suo</i><br/>
<i>Prolem marito iam senior Sara,</i><br/>
<i>Vltro ipsa seruam tradidit Abrahæ,</i><br/>
<i>Si forte tali coniugio placens</i><br/>
<i>Nascatur hares, cui sua linquerēt</i><br/>
<i>Post fata grandes diuitias pater.</i>
    </p>
    <p>
<i>Hac Ismaelem serua tulit ferum,</i><br/>
<i>Cui regna seclis post venientibus</i><br/>
<i>Promisit arcus sydereæ potens,</i><br/>
<i>Censusque opimos, &amp; varium decus.</i><br/>
<i>Sacris sed ipsa ad mancipium adibus</i><br/>
<i>Exire iussit, legitimum ut viro</i>
    </p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed text is partly damaged at the right edge of the stanzas; a few words are doubtful, e.g. "totaque totius" in line 6 of the second stanza, "sua" and "linquerēt" may be misread. The text continues past the bottom of the page.</notes>
